{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields","id":1029579,"title":"Force Fields","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T06:46:13-08:00","id":1029579,"title":"Force Fields","content":"How lenient are you with force field effects?<br /> <br /> Obviously there are numerous types and styles but for common Forces 2, Life 2, 3 or 4 (whatever you require to link in to a person so it moves) force fields whats your preferred method, as a ST specifically?<br /> <br /> I used to simply have them negate attack roll successes based on the Damage and Duration chart, as I assume most of us do. Lately I've gone even simpler and just have them negate 1 attack per success with 1 type of attack per success being effected. So 5 succeses would effect 4 attacks from say bullets and give it a days duration. I know this seems WAY too powerful on the surface but honeslty if non magical attacks are wasting your Mage when you are prepared for combat then you are doing something wrong. Of course this type of force field effect is totally vulgar. <br /> <br /> Oh, and I don't tend to have Force Fields act strangley with the surroundings. Aside from being more trouble than its worth most times I figure if it is counting as an active effect the Mage is maintaining he can manipulate it enough to not react off beat with the environment. And I find simple is better, and more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T12:13:28-08:00","id":1029690,"title":"","content":"For Forces 2. I tend to default to dividing successes into soak and duration. Each success gives them one die of soak from their selected energy source, be that Fire, Cold, Electricity, Harsh wind, or what have you.<br /> <br /> Yes this means that successes made to harm a mage with forces add up to more than they do to protect a mage from forces using the sphere, but for me that's where Countermagic steps in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T22:40:04-08:00","id":1029926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields#post1029579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How lenient are you with force field effects?<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> I used to simply have them negate attack roll successes based on the Damage and Duration chart, as I assume most of us do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's obvious a way to do it. Let me list a few:<br /> <br /> Types of absorption:<br /> * Outright negates whole attacks, X times where X is Arete roll successes. I think that's quite too powerful. That'd stop nukes with Forces 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> * Automatically Negates attacks based on damage/duration chart. Quite powerful.<br /> * Negates based on a 1-to-1 success amount instead of duration chart.<br /> * Soaks attacks based on damage/duration chart. Realistically probably tied with the above, but requires more Arete successes to get to the same level.<br /> * Soaks based on 1-to-1 success amount. Weakest version.<br /> <br /> Duration:<br /> * Normal duration (With the exception of the X attacks topmost bullet point)<br /> * Ablative, negating/soaking/attacks also reduce duration successes, or at least reduce leftover soak/negation successes. Weaker.<br /> <br /> And I think that's pretty much it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I've seen all sorts of versions and mixtures of the above being done by STs in the past..with the most annoying being an ablative duration, 1-to-1 forcefield in Revised - It was an orgy of ritual dice rolls to get an adequate forcefield up that was supposed to last longer than one or two combat rounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I am a fan of normal-duration, 1-to-1 soaking fields. It means low-Arete characters can quickly get a couple of soak dice, but high Arete characters won't automatically get like a 6-7 auto-negation force aura with a fingersnip.<br /> <br /> An okay alternative would be ablative forcefields that use the damage chart and either soak or negate. Keep it 1-to-1 with normal duration, or ablative with the damage chart. I think that's a good balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-11-2017, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T23:34:16-08:00","id":1029943,"title":"","content":"* Soaks based on 1-to-1 success amount. Weakest version.<br /> <br /> ^This.<br /> <br /> You gotta keep in mind it's just Forces 2, can't be that powerful to stop any attack or else Forces 2 is just an easy-to-get alternative to solve a lot of Mage's problems, literally everyone would try to get that. I rule it out (and as far as I remember, it goes like that in RAW too) that for melee attacks, each success on Arete roll substracts one success from melee attack successes. You score 3 successes on Arete and That Bad Guy scores 3 successes on attack, and you're safe. Should he score 4+ successes, you get slapped (unless you also dodge on top of that, etcetera). As for ranged attacks, it states that /mundane/ ranged attacks (someone shooting at you, someone firing arrows at you) are stopped at rate of: 1 projectile if 2 successes, many projectiles if 3 successes.<br /> <br /> Duration goes according to duration chart, of course, but do I /really/ have to tell you that walking around entire day with forcefield around you is a bad, and very stupid idea? You're basically shouting &quot;hello, I'm supernatural, I bump everything from distance&quot;. You cannot handshake someone, because their hand bumps in your forcefield. You approach to grab something but it just flies away (at best, might as well be something else unpredictable). Hell, your clothes might react weird to it, unless you've got Matter or already were wearing something. Basically, it's troublesome to just walk around with it for extended periods of time.<br /> <br /> The better alternative are wards due to much less side-effects, but wards require an established mage with many Spheres (or else you'll be leaving a lot of gaps to make it not-so-cool), but even then, you'd require ton of successes + Quintessence to ban many-many things away from yourself (again, gaps). Anyone who's got some info on you and is smart enough about it can give it a try to bypass your defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:34:58-08:00","id":1030011,"title":"","content":"Well you cant stop Nukes with Forces 2, that would be Forces 5. But ya, I see your point. <br /> <br /> The only real problem I have with the way I'm doing it is keeping track of the types of Forces protected againt. Treating successess as Soak dice, something we haven't really done is probably less note tracking. <br /> <br /> Thanks guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:45:03-08:00","id":1031579,"title":"","content":"This is exactly what I like to use Rotes for, describing exact Effects and the rules regarding them and working off the Magnitude of Effect chart instead of the Dam&amp;Dur charts etc. For example in my current game I have a player who's Virtual Adept Character has developed a Rote that takes the form of a coat that has a reality coded &quot;displace&quot; program running through it's inlaid circuitry with a &quot;return to sender&quot; trajectory algorithm also programmed into it's function. It's a Matter 2 Corr 2 Forces 2 effect that teleports bullets around his person and on enough successes can even 'fire' the bullets (and arrows and other solid matter projectiles) back in the direction they came. <br /> <br /> Functionally this is typically takes the form of extended casting to config the coat for use and requires 7 successes, the results of which make the wearer immune to bullets, arrows and any other fast moving 'ballistics' and also generates a 2 dice attack back at the target at diff 8. It's also not very coincidental and rapidly racks up Domino Effect in a firefight. Of course any damage to the coat causes the systems to short out and renders the rote useless. <br /> <br /> Similarly is an Bad Luck field that is used by the cabal's Dreamspeaker. She has a coin/poker chip that she flips and whispers to invoking the spirits of fortune to watch over her and curse her enemies. This is Entropy 2, Corr 2 and requires 5 successes. The first 3 actions of Harmful intent that target the character suffers -3 successes on their roll. Once that is done it is done and the spirits can not be roused to watch over her for another day. <br /> <br /> The Charts are really handy for working out on the fly or baselines of effects but there are some cool and inventive stuff that can be done with Rotes that doesnt have to fit with just the Chart results (several published rotes tend to do their own thing for example.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:16:00-08:00","id":1031697,"title":"","content":"Rotes are awsome for nailing down specifics on how things will work. However we never use them. Instead I have a few examples of how the mechanics of certain often used effects will be handled, and even those aren't concrete. Actually even the force field effect I mentioned is 1 of 5 or 6 ways we do it depending on the circumstances. It ws just the primary way I was handling continous moving fields. Which we have since ditched for saok dice as mentioned simply for less note taking as I just allow the field to soak anything Forces 2 can reasonably effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:44:21-08:00","id":1031711,"title":"","content":"Generally, I allow them to negate damage, not attacks. And at the same rate you would DEAL damage with them.<br /> <br /> So you get shot in the face. It hits. Your forcefield would then negate 2 damage per success on the arete roll to put it up and continue to do so for the duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T15:32:46-08:00","id":1033687,"title":"","content":"You'll need Entropy to make force fields that don't bump into things.<br /> <br /> But, if you have Entropy 2, I see no reason to make force fields at all... Them bullets will simply miss you all the time by few inches....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:11:28-08:00","id":1033709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields?p=1033687#post1033687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll need Entropy to make force fields that don't bump into things.<br /> <br /> But, if you have Entropy 2, I see no reason to make force fields at all... Them bullets will simply miss you all the time by few inches....</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you need Entropy to make force fields that don't bump into things? Life would be sufficient. I mean unless you're making it like an inch away from your skin for some reason. Which is dumb. It should be like a second skin of invincible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:07:37-08:00","id":1033739,"title":"","content":"You don't need life for that. Life would be for turning your skin into a force field (damn, would you look ugly!). That's not how spheres work; you'll only use life if you change your life pattern. To make a force field touching your skin, you'll only need forces, maybe just a few more successes and that's all. Still, you can't grab anything while it is on.<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 is the classic &quot;trigger&quot; you'll put on any spell. For example, Spirit 4, Entropy 2, to ward against any wraith, except one that has commited suicide. Or making a force field that only &quot;gets on&quot; against potencial threats (maybe your etherite builds a force field that is only activated under stress. When the levels of adrenaline in your blood drops, the field is deactivated). Or a portal that lets anyone pass except someone named Rumpelstistikin. And so on.<br /> <br /> By the way, Entropy 2 is the best thing there is in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:44:08-08:00","id":1033766,"title":"","content":"Errr.... no. The stress one would be Forces Life, because it's scanning your life pattern and activating or deactivating based on what it finds. Entropy is for destiny manipulation and probability.<br /> <br /> Life is for bonding the forcefield to your living pattern so that it moves with your pattern without you shaping the forces constantly or leaving it in a big shapeless bubble around you. Forces X Life 2.<br /> <br /> Also, that would be Spirit 2, Correspondence 3, possibly mind 2 for the suicide component or possibly as a freebie.<br /> <br /> That last one is also Correspondence 3 plus Mind 2-3. Correspondence 3 to both set up the portal and the ban, Mind 2-3 to enforce detect and engage the ban.<br /> <br /> Entropy would be something like Entropy X Time 2 Forces 3 to light anyone with an above average chance of killing me in the next five seconds on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:42:05-08:00","id":1034140,"title":"","content":"There is a great deal of misconception about Entropy. Indeed, it's the hardest sphere to understand. Let me try to shed some light on it<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 is the basic &quot;conditional trigger&quot; in ANY effect. If you know anything about computer language, its the most simple &quot;if, else, or, and&quot; codes.<br /> <br /> If X, than A.<br /> If Y, than B.<br /> If Z and W, than C.<br /> If K or J, than D.<br /> <br /> To say that you need Mind 3 to &quot;read the mind&quot; of all wraiths to determine which ones commited suicide to trigger an effect instead of using Entropy 2 for the &quot;suicidal&quot; trigger, is just as absurd as saying that you would ALWAYS need Matter to use Entropy 3, Life for Entropy 4 or Mind for Entropy 5. And that makes no sense.<br /> <br /> For example, I use Entropy 5 to make agent 234 defect to the Traditions. Very well. I'm succesful, I accumulate 20 succeses, all is fine and good. The agent WILL become a traditionalist.<br /> <br /> But... How will that happen?<br /> <br /> Well, perhaps on his next mission, he is sent to &quot;neutralize&quot; a Verbena girl. But, when he meets her, she reminds him of his deceased sister (who were killed by nephandi in a blood ritual, and the reason for him having joined the Union). After sending her to room 101, something begins to change in the agents heart... He start questioning many things about his own life. Later on, he is sent against a nefandi cult. Things go badly this time; still shacked by the capture of the Verbena girl, agent 234 acts on impulse in an emotional outburst of anger, and endangers the mission (causing the death of two other agents). The commander officer of the mission betrays him at his most fragile moment, saying &quot;you are a disgrace for the Union!&quot; and cowardly flees, only to be able to save his own skin and using this &quot;inciddent&quot; as an excuse to undermine the political position of agent's 234 mentor &quot;for recommending such an instable individual&quot;. Agent 234 survives, but is now bitter about the bureoucracy of the Union. In his next and last mission, agent 234, now demoted to the Low rank of a MiB, is saved by a charismatic and kind Etherite that reminds him of his old father, and the long lost time of his childhood were he had a happy life with his family.<br /> <br /> Agent 234 is no longer an agent after that, instead finding new meaning in his life as Professor Agentor (his new secret ID)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:03:58-08:00","id":1034157,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> <br /> Without touching all of your writing let me just say that your reading of Entropy is very much too powerful for the most mage players out there.<br /> After all even if the 2nd dot of Entropy is a basic universal trigger, then there is still the sensors and other things to consider.<br /> <br /> If you concentrate on your forcefield then you do not bother with additional spheres, you actively maintain the borders of your field to form as needed.<br /> RAW it is a possibility to lock the effect with Life 3 to yourself or Life 4 to others. This doesn't in itself make the forcefield necessarily any less cumbersome to wield in close quarters.<br /> <br /> A forcefield that only activates if needed should employ Time 4 as a way to hang the effect and your choice of effects to detect danger. On top an effect to put the forcefield to sleep if not needed.<br /> It is much better to bind a spirit in a fetish for such a task. (IMHO)<br /> <br /> Many Spheres are only the best if you happen to have a ST who thinks likewise.<br /> I've seen examples in which Spirit 2 easily was way better than any of the other spheres, because some spirit did the stuff for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:05:42-08:00","id":1034158,"title":"","content":"See? I never manipulated agent's 234 mind to make him change... It all happened by chance, I simply gave a push on Destiny. I didn't use Mind to brainwash him.<br /> <br /> The same holds true for any other levels of Entropy. Its all by &quot;happenstance&quot;. Entropy NEVER gives direct control over patters.<br /> <br /> That being said, I DON'T need mind 3 to set the &quot;suicidal&quot; trigger. Nor the &quot;adrenalin&quot; trigger either (an important note is that when I reffered to &quot;adrenalin&quot; as a trigger, that's much more about paradigm coloring the effect than actual biochemestry conditon. A Akashic could do exactly the same by labelling the trigger &quot;X will happen when my Chi suffers an imbalance&quot;. That also doesn't need Life either). The Mage DOESN'T NEED TO KNOW WHEN A SUICIDAL WRAITH CROSSES HIS WARD.<br /> <br /> Destiny (with capital &quot;D&quot; knows).<br /> <br /> In fact, Entropy 2 as all about conditinal effects.<br /> <br /> If, Else<br /> <br /> &quot;If a suicidal wraith crosses this line, trigger the Spirit 4 effect that I placed. Else, do nothing&quot;<br /> <br /> When I use Entropy 2 to manipulate luck, for example, Im doing just that. Most people just don't see the cause/consequence chain of events, becausr they are being simult\u00e2neos, but:<br /> <br /> &quot;If I cast this dice, the result will be 6. Else, if my opponent cast it, it will be 1&quot;.<br /> <br /> Its the SAME principle for ANY Entropy 2 effect. It's basical cause/consequence manipulation of a chain of events.<br /> <br /> But, in the same way that I don't need Forces 1, Matter 1 and perhaps Corr 1 and Time 1 to be able to calculate the exact mass, speed, angle, momentum, atrittion, and any other parameters that would allow me to calculate precisely the amount of Forces 2 that I would need to set a dice result, similarly I don't need Mind to scan for suicidals (actually, I can use Entropy 1 to tell the <i>causa mortis</i> of every wraiths of Stygia)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:25:11-08:00","id":1034166,"title":"","content":"Im pretty sure RAW requires Entropy 3 for conditonal triggers which is mentioned with Time 4 triggers. Dont have books atm but i remember it always being this way.<br /> Edit: HDYDT page 113. I'm pretty sure it's mentioned elsewhere as well<br /> <br /> And Entropy 3 and 4 most certainly give direct control over physical and living paterns. Even the sphere descriptor says it plainly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 01-18-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:32:58-08:00","id":1034172,"title":"","content":"My point is that Entropy 2 on its own can not activate(trigger) an effect, thats what you need Time 4 for.<br /> Otherwise, by extension why even bother with other spheres at all?<br /> &quot;If a wraith comes around, the result will be that he or she will not cross this line. Else, if it is a suicidal wraith, the line may be traversed&quot;<br /> Mind you, I like Entropy, a lot actually, but you do it a disservice if it is a &quot;must have&quot;.<br /> <br /> I try to make all spheres worthwhile without making any a no brainer to pick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:21:17-08:00","id":1034340,"title":"","content":"Disregarding M20 because their sphere requirements are literally nonsensical. Honestly their rules for magic in general are nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Entropy manipulates CHANCE. It takes a 10% chance and turns it into a 90-100% chance. Or Vice Versa. As you grow in power you go from being able to see chance, to being able to affect the chaos within static objects, to being able to manipulate the chances within dynamic objects etc etc until eventually you're able to manipulate chance in time and space. Why on earth would it be required for a conditional trigger?<br /> <br /> Out of ANY sphere, that would be mind. But that's still asinine and stupid. You build a spell. It has two parts. It has a Life 2 effect that detects how healthy you are. And a correspondence effect to teleport you home if you're seriously injured. And life 3 to lock it to your pattern. You put enough successes into duration to keep the spell going in perpetuity.<br /> <br /> It's not a 'hanging effect' which would require time 4 to do. It's a constantly running buff. Why would you need a magic that manipulates chance to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:30:55-08:00","id":1034346,"title":"","content":"With that reasoning why do I need any sphere beyond Prime. It manipulates the threads of quintessence. Everything is made up of quintessence, even magic manipulates quintessence. With Prime I can pull on the quintessential paterns of all reality thus manipulating all things. I have no reason for any other sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:34:00-08:00","id":1034347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields?p=1034346#post1034346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that reasoning why do I need any sphere beyond Prime. It manipulates the threads of quintessence. Everything is made up of quintessence, even magic manipulates quintessence. With Prime I can pull on the quintessential paterns of all reality thus manipulating all things. I have no reason for any other sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime manipulates <i>RAW</i> quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:02:58-08:00","id":1034360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields?p=1034347#post1034347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prime manipulates <i>RAW</i> quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the lower levels yes not at 4 and 5. <br /> <br /> You really think it's a good idea for spells to have a mind of their own. Thats what you want your life spell to do. Life manipulates living paterns, it doesn't make decisions based on the results of said paterns. But combing a contingent Entropy 3 effect or giving it sentience through Mind 5 it can inact an effect that was delayed through Time 4. <br /> <br /> Just Prime or Life or just any 1 sphere can't do it all. Other spheres are required. I'm not really sure why that's an issue since Mages don't focus on just 1 sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T18:31:14-08:00","id":1034379,"title":"","content":"Except Entropy doesn't <i>do</i> contingencies. It simply doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have a mind, you have a mind, and you build it to do what you want it to do.<br /> <br /> And I never said one sphere can do it all. But you don't need other spheres <i>just to use the effects of the spheres you actually have.</i> Life magic can detect your state of health, and heal you. Therefor, it's nonsensical to require another sphere dealing with something else entirely to make a spell that monitors your state of health and heals you if it stops being what it's supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Also Time 4 is for HANGING effects. Where you cast a spell, don't roll for duration and then stick it into frozen time to use later. I'm talking about long lasting spells with durations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T22:06:17-08:00","id":1034460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029579-force-fields?p=1034340#post1034340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy manipulates CHANCE. It takes a 10% chance and turns it into a 90-100% chance. Or Vice Versa. As you grow in power you go from being able to see chance, to being able to affect the chaos within static objects, to being able to manipulate the chances within dynamic objects etc etc until eventually you're able to manipulate chance in time and space. Why on earth would it be required for a conditional trigger?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Entropy manipulates <i>Fate and Fortune</i>. This does include chance, but it also includes events. It reads and changes your <i>Fate</i>. This is why you need it conjunctional with a Time 4 spell. If you just have Time 4, it hangs the Effect, but only for a set duration. It will go off when the time comes, and only then. With Entropy 3, you tie it the hung spell, not to a set time in the future, but to a particular twist of fate, a chosen eventuality. Time doesn't deal with destiny or fortune, only time's passage. Time may measure out the thread of history, but Entropy determines how that thread is weaved.<br /> <br /> This is not an invention of M20, either. It's been the case since at least Revised:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: The Ascension Revised Core, p. 191</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Entropy, a bit of Time magic can create an Effect that does not happen until a certain crux of destiny or improbability comes to pass. A princess can be put to sleep until her predestined true love arrives or a dying subject can be placed into cryogenic suspension while doctors search for a cure for his condition. Entire family lines or places of power can have magical Effects granted that wait until they're signaled for activation, though use and the rigors of Paradox slowly erode such Effects until they're gone.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're quoting the Revised handbook, the Entropy Sphere is listed with the following Specialties: Chaos, Dissolution, Fate, Fortune, Order.<br /> <br /> So I'm not pulling that out of my ass either, nor is it a recent addition of M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}